		// own type columns — there is no second array and no copy-back at the end of the body. It is
		// safe because both are re-created (not cleared) for the next function, so nothing aliases
		// these afterwards. See IrFunction.valueTags / valueNameIds for what the columns are FOR.
		var func = IrFunction.create(name, maxonReturnType: returnType, paramCount: paramCount, maxonParamTypes: paramTypes, valueTags: self.valueTags, valueNameIds: self.valueNameIds, valueClosureEnv: self.valueClosureEnv, valueIsCapturingClosure: self.valueIsCapturingClosure, valueWitnessIds: self.valueWitnessIds, returnLine: nameTok.line, declaredAt: SourcePosition.declaredAt(self.filePath, nameTok: nameTok), throwsTypeName: throwsClause)
		func.visibility = visibility

		// ⭐ **THE FUNCTION IS PUSHED UP FRONT, NOT AT THE END, AND THAT IS WHAT MAKES ValueOrigin CORRECT
