		// constraint witness under the PREVIOUS function's index — while `bindParameters`, ten lines below,
		// files the USER parameters correctly and says in its own comment that the order is why. So a hidden
		// slot resolved to no source span in the function that actually owned it.
		// **MEASURED: `panic at RegisterPressureDiagnostic.maxon:482: register-pressure E5001: value 2 …
		// resolves to NO source span — not a parameter …`**, on a one-parameter generic hash table's `grow()`,
		// where value 2 is the constraint-witness slot. That diagnostic's RULE 3 reads a missing span as "a
		// compiler-introduced value is blocking an allocation" and aborts — so a misfiled ORIGIN presented as
		// a register-allocator bug. The columns are still seeded in ABI order
		// (`[user][env][existentialWitness][layout][constraintWitness]`) because that is what this block's own
		// order is; only the FILING moved, and it moved to the one point where the index is this function's.
